# Student submissions never belong in this repo: it is public, and the
# dashboard reads it over raw.githubusercontent.com. The agent fetches them
# into its own data/responses/ instead. This stays as a backstop for a stray
# copy, and ignores the whole directory rather than one extension — the old
# per-phase rules covered *.md in some phases, everything in others, and
# phase 6 had no rule at all.
**/responses/
**/agent_state/
**/.canvas_fetch_index.json

# Neither does the grading key. `standards/phase_N.csv` says what state of the
# world closes each incident; the dashboard reads this repo over
# raw.githubusercontent.com, so a copy here is the answers, published. It lives
# in the agent's own private repo, tracked. This is the backstop, not the rule.
**/standards*.csv
standards/
